package audit

// admindoors.go — Spec 133 FR-022: the door registry. Every administrative
// door the proxy registers — each chi route and method of the personal REST
// router, each built-in MCP tool, each runnable CLI command — is listed here,
// per effect branch, as done (it writes the named admin_action lines),
// pending (a later slice of the plan writes them) or exempt (no committed
// effect, with the reason from contract §Exempt).
//
// Enumeration tests in internal/httpapi, internal/server and cmd/mcpproxy
// walk the production registrations and fail when a door is missing here or
// an entry no longer exists, so a new door cannot merge without a record.
// TestAdminDoorRegistry_PendingOnlyShrinks pins the pending set by identity
// (AdminDoorsFrozenPending, admindoors_pending.go): a slice that ships lines
// flips its rows to done and removes them from the frozen list; a new pending
// row has to be added to that list, visibly, in review.
//
// Branches inside a door (a flag split in RunE, a cascade in a service)
// cannot be discovered by enumeration; they are listed per door here and
// pinned by the exact-effect door table tests (FR-023).
//
// Scope note (PR-1a): REST doors are the personal-edition router's; the
// server-edition sibling group, the outer http.ServeMux registrations (MCP
// mounts, /oauth/*, callbacks) and per-surface MCP registrations are
// enumerated from PR-1b on (specs/133-admin-action-audit/plan.md).

// DoorStatus is a registry row's state.
type DoorStatus string

const (
	DoorDone    DoorStatus = "done"
	DoorPending DoorStatus = "pending"
	DoorExempt  DoorStatus = "exempt"
)

// AdminDoor is one (door, branch) row.
type AdminDoor struct {
	// Door is "REST <METHOD> <chi pattern>", "MCP <tool>" or "CLI <command path>".
	Door string
	// Branch names an effect branch inside the door; "" is the whole door.
	Branch  string
	Status  DoorStatus
	Slice   string // the plan slice that owns (or will own) the lines
	Actions []string
	Reason  string
}

